    "Working - Studying | ZHAW University Library\nSearch for\nDelete search term\nSearch\nWorking - Studying\nApart from a comprehensive range of print and electronic media, our library locations provide a modern infrastructure for students, researchers and lecturers.\nWinterthur\nZurich\nWädenswil\nAny location\n“I often use the University Library to find inspiration from newly published articles in journals or specialist publications.”\nRegula Treichler Bratschi, Research Associate\n«The fantastic library team and their expertise down to the last detail, as well as the extensive, well-maintained and easily accessible collection of sources are what make the library the heart of the Toni Areal campus in my opinion!»\nDr. Tim Tausendfreund, lecturer\n«I appreciate the highly competent support of the always helpful and friendly staff at the University Library, both as someone who uses its services and as a subject-matter expert.»\nDr. Sabine Steiger-Sackmann, lecturer and R&D area manager\nPrevious\nNext\nThe Tista Murk building on the Sulzer site, which extends over approximately 6000 square metres, offers a modern media, information and study environment.\nUniversity Library Winterthur\nWorking in the study environment\nLibrary\nMon to Fri 8 a.m.–7 p.m.\nSat 9 a.m.–5 p.m.\nLibrary and Self Services open to the public\nStaffed opening hours\nMon to Fri 9 a.m.–6 p.m.\nSat 9 a.m.–5 p.m.\nAdvice, collection and return of media\nat the information desk\ncash payment of library fees\nBuilding incl. study environment\nfor ZHAW members\nMon to Sun 7 a.m.–12 a.m. (midnight)\nBuilding incl. study environment\nfor external users\nMon to Sat 7 a.m.–7 p.m.\nFor reference service, see\nthe respective consulting hours\n.\nEvent and period\nLibrary\nBuilding incl. study environment\nReduced opening hours before Christmas\nWednesday, 23 December 2026 from 8 a.m.–5 p.m, staffed from 9 a.m–4 p.m.\nZHAW members and public 7 a.m.-7 p.m.\nThe University Library Zurich on the Toni Areal campus, together with the\nMedia and Information Centre (MIZ)\n, offers ZHAW members a centralised media, study and search location.\nUniversity Library Zurich\nMonday to Friday\n9 a.m.–7 p.m.\nSaturday\n10 a.m.–4 p.m.\nFor reference service, see\nthe respective consulting hours\n.\nInternal event\nWednesday, 9 December 2026\nClosed from 5 p.m.\nChristmas and New Year holiday\nThursday, 24 December 2026 to Sunday, 3 January 2027\nClosed\nThe ZHAW University Library Wädenswil is a specialised library focussing on life sciences and facility management. It offers students and researchers a place to work, study and conduct searches.\nUniversity Library Wädenswil\nStaffed opening hours\nMon to Fri 9 a.m.–1 p.m. and 2 p.m–4 p.m.\nLibrary and Self Services open to the public\nOpen Library for all\nMon to Fri 7 a.m.–7 p.m.\nLibrary and Self Services open to the public\nOpen Library for ZHAW students\nMon to Sun 7 a.m.–12 a.m. (midnight)\nLibrary and Self Services accessible with CampusCard\nOpen Library for ZHAW staff\nMon to Sun 24/7\nLibrary and Self Services accessible with CampusCard\nFor reference service, see\nthe respective consulting hours\n.\nChristmas holiday\nThursday, 24 December 2026 to Wednesday, 30 December 2026\nClosed\nOpen Library accessible to ZHAW students and staff, closed to the public\nNew Year holiday\nThursday, 31 December 2026 to Friday, 1 January 2027\nClosed\nOpen Library closed for ZHAW students and the public, accessible to staff\nAs a member of the ZHAW you can work and study anywhere and at the same time make use of our wide range of electronic media. All the e-media licensed by the ZHAW is accessible via VPN connection from any location.\nVPN\nInstructions in the Self Service Portal (ZHAW login required)\n­\nWith some suppliers, access is also possible via Shibboleth.  Select “Institutional Login” and then “ZHAW” on the supplier’s website. Then log in with your Switch edu-ID.\nPlease note that you will only be logged onto this specific platform, so you won’t be able to access any other electronic media. If you want to have access to other licensed resources, please connect via VPN."
